//@version=6
// BTC ATTACK 55 - FUNDING-SETTLEMENT SQUEEZE REVERSION, RANGE REQUIREMENT DROPPED. LONG LEG.
//
// THE STORED PROMPT still asks for Attack 37's filter stack (a NINTH time now), describing a board
// state (Attack 37, 322/196 trades, "earned a filter stack, queued not built") that is 18 attacks
// stale. THE DOCS OVERRIDE IT, again: Attack 41 closed Attack 37 as a development target, Attack 43
// closed the whole sweep-reversal FAMILY (37-43), Attack 47 -- the one filter tried on the current
// champion, Attack 46 -- died on the ~77% sample wall (HARD LESSON 45/49). This cycle instead executes
// Attack 54's own queue item 1, which explicitly outranks inventing a sixth clock-based variant or a
// wholly new mechanism: "if the funding-clock family is revisited, drop the elevated-range requirement
// first and measure frequency alone before adding any second condition back."
//
// ==================== WHAT CHANGED FROM ATTACK 54, AND ONLY THIS ====================
// Attack 54 required THREE independent same-bar conditions: settlement clock, elevated range
// (ta.tr >= 1.5x its trailing 20-bar average), and a down close. It got 7 trades on H1 -- ~38x rarer
// than its own pre-registered ~270 estimate, the largest frequency miss yet recorded on this board.
// Attack 54's own diagnosis: "whichever pairwise correlation was assumed independent was not,
// most plausibly because settlement-timestamp bars do not carry meaningfully different range statistics
// than any other bar once the trailing-average normalisation is applied, so requiring 1.5x on top of
// the exact-minute clock condition stacks two nearly-orthogonal rare events." This cycle tests that
// diagnosis directly: `rangeBig` is REMOVED. `isSettlement` and `isBigDown` are UNCHANGED, bit-for-bit
// identical to Attack 54 (`hourUTC`/`minuteUTC` arithmetic, `isBigDown = close < open`). Stop, target,
// R floor, maxBars, sizing, commission -- all identical to Attack 54. This is a single-term removal on
// the existing base, not a new mechanism.
//
// ==================== THE CLAIM, NARROWED ====================
// Every 15m bar whose OPEN lands exactly on a funding-settlement timestamp (00:00/08:00/16:00 UTC) and
// which closes below its own open is candidate forced-flow selling synchronised to the settlement
// clock, independent of how large that bar's range is relative to its own recent history. If Attack
// 54's diagnosis is right, this measures the settlement-clock effect at its full, un-compounded
// frequency; if the clock itself carries no directional edge once the range filter is removed, PF
// should sit near the funding-agnostic baseline (no better than an unconditional down-bar fade), which
// this run will show directly rather than assume.
//
// ==================== AUDIT, ONE LINE PER LEG (LONG ONLY -- LESSON 6) ====================
//   R >= 0.8% (LESSON 3) -- rFloorOk, close-to-low on the settlement bar, unchanged from Attack 54,
//        enforced by EXCLUSION (a shallow bar is skipped, never widened).
//   Stop beyond STRUCTURE (LESSON 5) -- slPx = the settlement bar's own low, unchanged from Attack 54.
//   Each leg separately (LESSON 6) -- LONG ONLY this cycle, identical scope declaration as Attack 54:
//        the short mirror (fading an oversized UP settlement bar) is a deliberate next step, not run
//        here, and funding mechanics remain directionally symmetric by construction (HARD LESSON 48
//        exempts this family, unlike price-structure support/resistance).
//   BINDING (E17) -- now TWO independent conditions on one bar (clock, down close) instead of three;
//        trade count is read before any ratio is quoted (LESSON 12), and this run's own point is to
//        measure how much removing the third term changes that count.
//   REDUNDANCY (E14) -- rFloorOk constrains STOP distance; rrOk only checks tpPx sits above close
//        (existence, not a size threshold). Non-overlapping, unchanged from Attack 54.
//   LATCH IN SEQUENCE (LESSON 8) -- N/A BY DESIGN, stated explicitly: both trigger conditions (clock,
//        direction) evaluate on ONE bar, no arm/trigger split to sequence.
//   SL and TP FIXED AT ENTRY -- slPx/tpPx captured once at entry, from the settlement bar's own low and
//        the preBars-back close (preBars=4, unchanged). No trailing, no averaging down, no martingale.
//   CASCADE (HARD LESSON 35/50) -- 100% equity, fixed stop/target; expect cascadeRatio 1 if this
//        advances far enough to need get_trades verification before RATCHET v2 clause 3.
//   WEEKENDS (structural note 4) -- funding settles identically on weekends; no special-casing.
//
// ==================== FREQUENCY ESTIMATE, A HYPOTHESIS TO BE SCORED (HARD LESSON 4) ====================
// Settlement bars are 1-in-32 (~5,115 of ~163,700 15m bars over the full window). Naive independence
// with a ~50% down-bar fraction gives ~2,560 candidate bars full-sample, split roughly by each half's
// bar count (~85,655 H1 / ~78,000 H2, Attack 43's own count) to something near 1,340 H1 / 1,220 H2
// before the R-floor trims further. THIS ESTIMATE IS FLAGGED IN ADVANCE AS LIKELY ABOVE THE LAB'S OWN
// SETTLED 60-350-PER-HALF WORKABLE BAND (Attack 33 died at 757 trades on cost) -- if the actual count
// lands far above 350, that is itself the finding this run exists to produce (HARD LESSON 4), and a
// PF that clears 1.0 gross but fails on commission drag would need the same cost-screen treatment
// Attack 33 got, not a filter-stack rescue.
//
// ==================== OUTCOMES REGISTERED BEFORE THE RUN (LESSON 17) ====================
//   * PRE-2024 HALF (H1, never-tuned, 2022-01-01 -> 2024-06-08) BELOW 1.0 -> KILL RULE. Discard, do NOT
//     run H2. Removing the range filter did not rescue the clock claim; the funding-clock family is
//     0-for-2 (Attack 54 too thin to classify, Attack 55 measured and negative).
//   * H1 >= 1.0 AND TRADE COUNT INSIDE OR NEAR THE 60-350 BAND -> run H2 as the second credit; a real
//     third both-halves-positive family candidate if H2 also clears 1.0.
//   * H1 >= 1.0 BUT TRADE COUNT FAR ABOVE 350 -> a cost problem in Attack 33's shape is likely; run H2
//     anyway (credits allow the full pair) but flag the cost screen as owed before any further work,
//     do not call it a candidate on PF alone.
//   * TRADE COUNT NEAR THE ~1,300 ESTIMATE -> confirms Attack 54's diagnosis that the range filter, not
//     the clock condition, was the source of the 38x miss. TRADE COUNT STILL FAR BELOW IT -> the clock
//     condition itself binds harder than assumed, a distinct and equally reportable finding.
//   * A MAJORITY OF HOLDS AT maxBars 192 -> HARD LESSON 38 truncation, reported before any conclusion
//     is drawn from the achieved win/loss ratio.
//   REPORT gross, commission, achieved ratio, avg loser, win rate and max drawdown together, per the
//   board's standing instruction since Attack 37 named the three drawdown categories.

strategy("BTC Attack55 funding settlement no-range", overlay=true,
     pyramiding=1, process_orders_on_close=true,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05,
     initial_capital=10000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=100,
     margin_long=100, margin_short=100)

preBars   = input.int(4,     "Bars before the settlement bar used as the target anchor (4 = 1h on 15m)")
minRpct   = input.float(0.80, "Min stop distance as % of price (LESSON 3)")
maxBars   = input.int(192,   "Max bars in trade")

hourUTC   = math.floor(time / 3600000) % 24     // hour() is unimplemented on this engine (Attack 50)
minuteUTC = math.floor(time / 60000) % 60

isSettlement = (hourUTC % 8 == 0) and (minuteUTC == 0)
isBigDown = close < open

signal = isSettlement and isBigDown

flat = strategy.position_size == 0

slCand = low
tpCand = close[preBars]

rLong    = close - slCand
minR     = close * minRpct / 100
rFloorOk = rLong >= minR
rrOk     = not na(tpCand) and tpCand > close

goLong = flat and signal and rFloorOk and rrOk

var float slPx   = na
var float tpPx   = na
var int   barsIn = 0

if flat and goLong
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
    slPx   := slCand
    tpPx   := tpCand
    barsIn := 0

if strategy.position_size > 0
    strategy.exit("LX", from_entry="L", stop=slPx, limit=tpPx)
    barsIn := barsIn + 1

if barsIn >= maxBars and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all()
    barsIn := 0

plot(goLong ? 1 : 0, title="LongSignal")
plot(slPx, title="StopPx")
plot(tpPx, title="TargetPx")
